{"ts": "2026-11-10T15:04:56.208133Z", "run_id": "r-20261110T1444Z-ede1", "unit": "openspec:add-policy-deploy", "seq": 33, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "The repository settles it: 0495_policy_sets.sql forces RLS with a current_setting('app.tenant_id', true) predicate; src/db/roles.ts creates both roles NOBYPASSRLS and test/support/global-setup.ts uses ensureRoles for the test cluster; src/tenancy/tx.ts sets the GUC only inside withTenantTx; the frozen test at lines 279 and 325 queries ownerPool without it; the test plan says rows() runs in T; src/tenancy/tx.test.ts already shows the owner connection needing the GUC on a forced-RLS table. The suggestion changes only the frozen test's query path and keeps the SQL, matching the plan.", "called": true, "tasks": ["3.4"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.573488, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "f7fb17918570b6ee427fdfbfc4930b178db427b71f10f02a93fc93d1036f574f", "checked": [{"ref": "src/grants/policy-deploy.test.ts:279", "quote": "const result = await f.db.ownerPool.query<Row>(", "claim": "The rows helper reads policy_set through the owner pool with no tenant setting."}, {"ref": "src/grants/policy-deploy.test.ts:325", "quote": "const stored = await f.db.ownerPool.query<{", "claim": "The stored-row query also reads policy_set through the owner pool without a tenant setting."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0495_policy_sets.sql:15", "quote": "ALTER TABLE ursitoare.policy_set FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;", "claim": "Row security is forced on policy_set, so the table owner is subject to the policy."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0495_policy_sets.sql:16", "quote": "USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id', true))", "claim": "With app.tenant_id unset the predicate is null and no row is visible."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0495_policy_sets.sql:17", "quote": "GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON TABLE ursitoare.policy_set TO ursitoare_app;", "claim": "The app role may SELECT the table, so the suggested withTenantTx reads work."}, {"ref": "src/db/roles.ts:12", "quote": "const ROLE_ATTRIBUTES = \"LOGIN NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE NOREPLICATION NOBYPASSRLS\";", "claim": "Both roles, the owner included, are created without BYPASSRLS."}, {"ref": "test/support/global-setup.ts:47", "quote": "await ensureRoles(adminPool, { ownerPassword, appPassword });", "claim": "The shared test cluster creates its roles with those attributes."}, {"ref": "src/tenancy/tx.ts:21", "quote": "await client.query(\"SELECT set_config('app.tenant_id', $1, true)\", [ctx.tenantId]);", "claim": "withTenantTx sets app.tenant_id inside the transaction, which the suggestion relies on."}, {"ref": "src/tenancy/tx.test.ts:84", "quote": "await client.query(\"SELECT set_config('app.tenant_id', $1, true)\", [tenantId]);", "claim": "An existing test sets the GUC even on an owner connection to write a forced-RLS table, confirming the owner does not bypass RLS."}, {"ref": "spec:test-plan-runtime.md", "quote": "`rows()` = `SELECT deploy_seq, version, current, deployed_at FROM ursitoare.policy_set ORDER BY deploy_seq` in T", "claim": "The test plan intends rows() to run in tenant T's context, as the suggestion does."}]}
