{"ts": "2026-11-10T15:07:09.104651Z", "run_id": "r-20261110T1444Z-ede1", "unit": "openspec:add-policy-deploy", "seq": 38, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-003", "id": "Q-003", "status": "answered", "reason": "Checked in the repository: the runtime builds the base engine without toolArgs and uses it for a tenant without a stored row; buildSchema then emits ToolArgs with only url and url_host; the invoke_tool action declares args: ToolArgs; runCheck calls statefulIsAuthorized with validateRequest true and maps a failure to PDP_REQUEST_INVALID; limits.test.ts proves an undeclared context attribute gives exactly that error; the frozen test's P helper puts amount into context.args; test-plan-runtime.md says the four non-L before-rows were derived, not run. The spec requires the base engine to decide such requests and does not state the before errors, so the suggested edit matches production behaviour and contradicts nothing. I could not run the test, but every link of the chain is in the code.", "called": true, "tasks": ["3.4"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.9694185000000004, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "661d77a14d42c5f02b20015b547abd41483d35fdb8133486aba48287578bce99", "checked": [{"ref": "src/grants/policy-runtime.ts:100", "quote": "const base = await createPolicyEngine({\n    srcDir: deps.srcDir,\n    clock: deps.clock,\n    ids: deps.ids,\n    logger: deps.logger,\n    instanceId: `${instance}/base`,", "claim": "The base engine is built with no toolArgs."}, {"ref": "src/grants/policy-runtime.ts:116", "quote": "if (stored === null) return { engine: base, toolArgs: {} };", "claim": "A tenant with no stored row is decided by the base engine."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/cedar-schema.ts:16", "quote": "[\"url\", \"String\"],\n    [\"url_host\", \"String\"],", "claim": "Without toolArgs the ToolArgs record declares only url and url_host."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/cedar-schema.ts:41", "quote": "return `type ToolArgs = { ${attributes} };`;", "claim": "ToolArgs is a closed Cedar record type with just the declared names."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/actions.ts:102", "quote": "\"{ tool: Tool, args: ToolArgs, taint: Set<String>, run_initiator: User,", "claim": "The invoke_tool context types args as ToolArgs, so an undeclared amount key is schema-invalid."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/check.ts:103", "quote": "validateRequest: true,", "claim": "Every check validates the request against the schema."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/check.ts:44", "quote": "if (answer.type === \"failure\") {\n    return denied(state, [], [\"PDP_REQUEST_INVALID\"]);", "claim": "A request validation failure is a deny with errors [\"PDP_REQUEST_INVALID\"] and reasons []."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/limits.test.ts:118", "quote": "const undeclaredAttribute = baseRequest();\n    undeclaredAttribute.context = { ...undeclaredAttribute.context, zzz: 1 };", "claim": "An existing test shows an undeclared context attribute yields PDP_REQUEST_INVALID."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/limits.test.ts:133", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(decision.errors, [\"PDP_REQUEST_INVALID\"]);", "claim": "That test asserts exactly the error the clarifier suggestion expects."}, {"ref": "src/grants/policy-deploy.test.ts:242", "quote": "const P = (amount: number, fp: string, approved = false): PolicyRequest =>\n  request(\"acme.create_payment@1\", \"pay\", \"pay\", fp, { amount: toDecimal(amount) }, approved);", "claim": "Every P request carries context.args.amount, which the base schema does not declare."}, {"ref": "src/grants/policy-deploy.test.ts:307", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(dec(await rt.engine.check(r)), [\"deny\", [], [], VBASE], `before: ${name}`);", "claim": "The frozen before loop expects empty errors for all five requests, including the four P ones."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-policy-deploy/test-plan-runtime.md:3", "quote": "**derived, not run**: the four other before-requests (§ Deploy decisions)", "claim": "The four P before-rows were never run when the test plan was written."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/policy-deploy/spec.md#requirement-a-tenants-layer-never-decides-another-tenants-request", "quote": "evaluate the request on that tenant's engine (its stored set, or the base engine without one)", "claim": "The spec requires the base engine, built without the tenant's argument types, to decide a tenant request before any deploy."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/policy-deploy/spec.md#scenario-a-deploy-stores-audits-and-swaps-the-tenants-engine", "quote": "the five decisions are those listed there, each carrying the validated version `V1`, while `rt.engine.policySetVersion` stays `VBASE`", "claim": "The spec lists only the after decisions, so changing the before P expectations contradicts no requirement."}]}
